  "conversion_warnings": [
    "Catalog year set to 2025-2026 per the live CourseLeaf program page (catalog.wku.edu).",
    "degree.id changed from '...-elective' to '...-computer-science' (skeletal id encoded a mis-classification of the program as an AI elective; this is the full BS CS major).",
    "cip_code 11.0701 (Computer Science) inferred from program name; not stated in catalog.",
    "Skeletal source modeled the major as a flat 'all' core plus a 'Math Electives' pick-2 and a stray 'AI Electives = CS456 all' / 'Unrestricted = MATH136 all'. Rebuilt to the catalog's two-track structure: General Option vs Systems/Scientific Applications Concentration, modeled as a type:one_of.",
    "General Option CS electives modeled as three select pools (3 hr 200+, 6 hr 300+, 3 hr 400+) per catalog wording 'Select 12 hours CS electives including: 3 hours at the 200-level or above (excluding CS 226 and CS 257), 6 hours at the 300-level or above and another 3 hours at the 400-level or above'. Excludes the 12 required core CS courses (and CS 226/CS 257 from the 200-level pool) so the pools draw only real electives.",
    "Systems/Scientific Applications Concentration electives are the explicit 12-hour list CS 270/315/372/381/443/445/446/450/456 plus 'choose two' advanced math/STAT from MATH 137/305/307/331/405/406/470/473, STAT 401/402 (6-8 hrs). This concentration totals ~121 hrs; total_credits=120 reflects the General Option graduation minimum (the stated lower bound).",
    "MATH 137 corrected to 4 credit_hours (live catalog) vs 3 in the skeletal source.",
    "MATH 136 (Calculus I) modeled as a supporting requirement (prereq for STAT 301 and CS 339); it also satisfies the Colonnade Quantitative Reasoning Foundation, so colonnade_foundations_quant carries external_credits=0 to avoid double-counting its 4 hours.",
    "WKU Colonnade general-education program (39 hrs: Foundations 18 + Explorations 12 + Connections 9) modeled as external_requirement select pools with '*:*' include patterns (per the avoid-PatternMatchesNoCourses rule), since specific Colonnade courses are not enumerated on the program page.",
    "Free/general electives = 24 hrs to reach 120 (120 - 41 core - 12 CS electives - 4 MATH136 - 39 Colonnade). Some general-elective hours absorb WKU's world-language proficiency requirement (novice-high before 60 hrs).",
    "Prerequisites de-listed of grade qualifiers ('with a minimum grade of C') and admission-standing phrases ('Human Communications', 'Writing in the Disciplines') which are not course references; CS360 and CS396 alternate paths (CS239/CS180[B]/EE380, ENG307) simplified to the primary CS-major path to avoid dangling external refs.",
    "CS180/CS290 placement-test prerequisite alternatives (ACT/SAT/MPE scores) dropped; only the course-based alternatives retained as boolean prereqs."
  ]
}